BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BOOK LAUNCH: DELE & AMINATA'S JOLLOF WAR\, by Yewande Daniel-Ayoad
 e and Bri Marie McNish
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261010T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261010T160000
UID:bm-6332420261010@adifferentbooklist.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/1188585/Book_Laun
 ch_Dele_and_Aminatas_Jollof_War.png?cb=1789072874
DESCRIPTION:📚🚀Want some delicious\, fragrant jollof rice? Then\, you
 're invited to join Yewande Daniel-Ayoade\, co-author of the new book DELE
  & AMINATA'S JOLLOF WAR\, for the launch of her picture book!\nEnfolded in
  DELE & AMINATA'S JOLLOF WAR\, a story about two African children\, Dele a
 nd Aminata\, who both believe that their versions of jollof rice are worth
 y of first prize at the neighbourhood competition\, is a note on the histo
 ry of the signature dish of West Africa\, plus a jollof rice recipe that c
 hildren will be excited to try!\nReaders will have the pleasure of listeni
 ng to Yewande read her story\, participating in a Q&A\, winning prizes\, a
 nd of course tasting some jollof rice and snacks inspired by the book!\nPr
 eorder DELE & AMINATA'S JOLLOF WAR\, by Yewande Daniel and Bri Marie McNis
 h (illus.) now\, or purchase it - and have it signed by the author at the 
 event.\nAdmission: Free.\nAll are welcome - #ReadDifferently and #EatDiffe
 rently!📚
LOCATION:BLACKHURST CULTURAL CENTRE
URL:https://adifferentbooklist.com/events
X-SOURCE:A Different Booklist
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Black & Caribbean Book Affair 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T200000
UID:bm-6512320261015@adifferentbooklist.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/1188585/FB_IMG_17
 91149019060.jpg?cb=1791149027
DESCRIPTION:📚Three days of books and ideas that reflect who we are!\n\n
 The Black & Caribbean Book Affair 2026 returns to Blackhurst CC from Oct 1
 5–17th  under the theme Seeing Ourselves: The Next Chapter.\n🔹Oct 15 
 | 6–8 PM\nDr. Carl James discusses Seeing Ourselves: Exploring Race\, Et
 hnicity & Culture\, 5th ed.\, with educators Marc Proudfoot and Ansar Dual
 eh.\n🔹Oct 16 | 6–8 PM\nRamie Veerappan joins Sandra Whiting for a con
 versation about Ramie’s Dance of Resilience: Apartheid and Beyond\, writ
 ten by Romila Logarahjah-Jeevithan.\n🔹Oct 17 | 9–10 AM on Zoom: Gelie
 n Matthews and Rhoma Spencer discuss Calypso Rose\, who broke through the 
 male-dominated calypso world.\n11 AM–1 PM: A Parade of Children’s Book
 s with Heather Beaumont\, Delano Brown and Yolanda Marshall.\n4:30–6:30 
 PM: Didier Leclair launches The African Prince\, the Translator\, and the 
 Nazi in conversation with Canute Lawrence.\nJoin us as Black & Caribbean s
 tories take centre stage!📚
LOCATION:Blackhurst Cultural Centre
URL:https://adifferentbooklist.com/events
X-SOURCE:A Different Booklist
END:VEVENT
