BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ROUNDTABLE DISCUSSION: LABOUR ACTIVISM AND DIVERSITY IN THE CONSTR
 UCTION INDUSTRY
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T203000
UID:bm-6539420261021@adifferentbooklist.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/1188585/Poster_Mi
 litants__Mobsters_and_Mavericks__4_261007_123820.jpg?cb=1791391123
DESCRIPTION:📚🚀🏗️You're invited to join historian Prof. Gilberto
  Fernandes for a discussion on labour activism and diversity in the const
 ruction industry. Labour leaders Rosemarie Powell\, Mamadou Bah and John 
 Cartwright will also join the panel.\nThe Canadian labour landscape is con
 stantly evolving because of various forces\, including law - think of the
  new Building Canada Strong Act - technology\, economy\, immigration. Prof
 . Fernandes's latest historical book MILITANTS\, MOBSTERS\, AND MAVERICKS\
 , which examines the explosive post-war labour growth in Toronto's constru
 ction industry in the '60s and '70s\, will serve as the stimulus for a bro
 ader discussion on the direction of work\, diversity\, and activism in Tor
 onto's construction industry.\nMILITANTS\, MOBSTERS\, AND MAVERICKS\, by P
 rof. Fernandes\, is on sale at A Different Booklist and will be available 
 for purchase at the event.\nAdmission: Free.\nJoin us for a constructive e
 xchange - #ReadDifferently!📚
LOCATION:Blackhurst Cultural Centre
URL:https://adifferentbooklist.com/events
X-SOURCE:A Different Booklist
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
